 of record since 1951, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids February to March came in under 90% of normal in 35 of them. In 2025 the middle ran 148% of normal in May to June and 66% in November to December. So far in 2026 it ran 61% in March to April, and grid 19983 shows a preliminary estimate of 75.1 for August to September 2026. Grid 19984 had its driest year in 2007 at 67%.</p>"}
